# As built the object of `dist` lies in a frame. Under DisableFrameCells, one of the two words of --aot-harden=proof-checks, a build takes the mechanism CellsInFrames away (withoutMechanismsThatOptionsWithhold()).
# testaot's staged commands did not: `walk` laid the cell in a frame, the emitter refused it, and no unit was printed. They ask the same function now: what they print under the word is what a build compiles.
# f0 = the file (dist and norm are copied in)
# RUN(BUILT): walk f0 mechanisms=all
# BUILT-LABEL: code f0:Body
# BUILT: NewObject {{*}}storage=Frame
# RUN(KEPT): walk f0 mechanisms=all testing=DisableFrameCells
# KEPT-LABEL: code f0:Body
# KEPT: NewObject
# KEPT-NOT: storage=Frame
